{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792798632,"nonce":"FWyMB/yWe7Vje6/rlCuNacimz6M=","title":"TypeScript: static string fields in records and classes","message":"Record types (aliases, interfaces, inline literals) and class fields may be strings. Every write to a string field stores a static string (a literal, a template of literal parts, a constant, a string enum member or a value read from another string field), so reads of string fields are static strings too and may be stored in arrays, unions and other fields. Strings built at run time and parameters stored in fields report \"string fields without a proven static lifetime\" Unsupported, matching the rule for string arrays. Templates of literal parts now lower to static string literals. Class fields initialized with a string literal infer string. New instances start their string fields as the empty string until the constructor assigns them.\n\nAlso corrected false Type errors that this work exposed: `\u0026\u0026` and `||` on non-boolean operands report Unsupported (value-selecting logic) instead of \"not assignable to boolean\"; console methods other than log, and console as a value, report Unsupported instead of \"cannot find name console\"; type members written on one line without `;` or `,` are a syntax error, as TypeScript reports (1005), which the parser did not enforce. The zyntax_ts snapshot test now checks the typed array GEP where the array escapes (pick's specialization) and that score releases every allocation it makes, since heap scalarization removes score's own arrays.\n\nOfficial corpus: PASS 947 -\u003e 979, FAIL 97, UNSUPPORTED 2360 -\u003e 2328, SKIP 3421; no crash, timeout or transition to FAIL. 33 new passes (rejections checked against the reference diagnostic at the same location; most are strict property initialization 2564 and readonly 2540 now reachable): classAppearsToHaveMembersOfObject, classExtendsShadowedConstructorFunction, allowUnescapedParagraphAndLineSeparatorsInStringLiteral, jsonRawJSON2, objectLiteralShorthandPropertiesFunctionArgument(2), templateStringInPropertyAssignment(ES6), comparisonOperatorWithNoRelationshipObjectsOnProperty, typeGuardOfFormTypeOf{Boolean,EqualEqualHasNoEffect,NotEqualHasNoEffect,Number,Other,String}, typeofOperatorWithStringType, importAliasIdentifiers, invalidImportAliasIdentifiers, parser509677, anyAsGenericFunctionCall, intersectionTypeReadonly, objectTypePropertyAccess, objectTypeLiteralSyntax, objectTypeLiteralSyntax2 (1005), invalid{Boolean,Number,String,Undefined}Assignments, arrayOfFunctionTypes3, typeofANonExportedType, typeofAnExportedType, unionTypePropertyAccessibility, unionTypeReadonly.\n\nOne false pass now Unsupported: expressions/binaryOperators/logicalAndOperator/logicalAndOperatorWithTypeParameters passed only on the false \"type T is not assignable to boolean\" for `t \u0026\u0026 t`; the reference's only error is 2454 elsewhere.\n\nParent: 5f1038edb654e4276e10f1d0870b261f397479f2f88710b5f1df265347474022.","files":null}]}